MaiPai Bot
Third-Party Licenses and Attributions

This is a fresh repo (the platform rebuild, see docs/dev.md). Components
declared as direct dependencies are attributed here, per docs/PACKAGES.md in
getmaipai/.github.

pyserial 3.5 (Chris Liechti), BSD-3-Clause. Declared in body/pyproject.toml;
used for the Reachy Eyes USB serial link. https://github.com/pyserial/pyserial

Pollen Robotics recorded moves, Apache-2.0. The optional moves package
plays motion files from the datasets reachy-mini-emotions-library and
reachy-mini-dances-library (https://huggingface.co/datasets/pollen-robotics),
credit to Pollen Robotics and Hugging Face. The files are never vendored:
the hub downloads them at a pinned revision with a sha256 checksum, and
only when the package is installed. The move format and the community
moves tag are Pollen's: reachy_mini_community_moves.

YuNet face detector (Wei Wu, Hanyang Peng, Shiqi Yu), MIT, as the unmodified OpenCV Zoo
model redistributed by Pollen Robotics (pollen-robotics/face_detection_yunet_2026may). The
hub syncs it at a pinned revision with a sha256 checksum; it is never vendored. The
decoding in body/maipai_body/vision/yunet.py follows reachy_mini.vision.face_detector
(Apache-2.0, Pollen Robotics).

Chatterbox Turbo (Resemble AI), Apache-2.0, as mlx-community/chatterbox-turbo-fp16 at the revision
the MaiPai Stack pins (b2d0a13aa7cfff0a06d9acb247ae91c8f19a6d75). It is the household's default
voice, and with it body/scripts/render_unit_phrases.py synthesizes the sixteen offline phrases the
StackChan says by itself when it has no link to Home (body/maipai_body/bodies/stackchan/firmware/
assets/phrases, firmware patch 118). The clips are machine-made speech, never a recording of a
person; the model is not redistributed here. The licence was checked against the Stack's pinned
catalog record on 2026-11-13 and is recorded in assets/phrases/phrases.json.

Pocket TTS (Kyutai), CC-BY-4.0, as pocket-tts-english (kyutai/pocket-tts-without-voice-cloning at
the revision the Stack pins). It renders the pre-rendered offline lines of the clip bundle
(body/maipai_body/speech/offline_clips.json). Credit line, carried in that manifest and in
docs/user/stackchan.md: "Voice generated with pocket-tts-english, licensed under CC-BY-4.0." The
licence was checked against the Stack's pinned catalog record on 2026-11-13.

The StackChan earcons (firmware/assets/sounds) are synthesized by body/scripts/render_unit_sounds.py
from sine waves: no recording, no third-party sound, MIT with the rest of this repo's firmware work.
